   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "ComfyUI 0.42.0 (commit 8f04fd6ec), web frontend 1.55.18, ComfyUI-MossPhoton 0.1.0.\n\nWorkflow: two Moss Photon LoRA Profile nodes chained through profile_in (MODEL and profile both go from the first node to the second), then the Sampler preset identity_safe.\n\nWeights (the workflow downloads nothing: download the files yourself and put them in these folders):\n- models/diffusion_models/moss_image_sft_bf16.safetensors (the official MOSS-Image-SFT bf16 file)\n- models/text_encoders/qwen3.5_9b_bf16.safetensors (the official Qwen3.5 9B bf16 text encoder of MOSS-Image; CLIPLoader type moss_image)\n- models/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors (Flux 2 VAE)\n- models/loras/your_character_lora.safetensors (PLACEHOLDER name: your character LoRA, applied first)\n- models/loras/your_second_lora.safetensors (PLACEHOLDER name: any second MOSS LoRA, role other)\n\nThe order of the nodes is the order of the patches and it changes the result in the last bits. The second adapter and both strengths (0.8 and 0.5) are PLACEHOLDERS for the chaining demo; no stack of two LoRAs has a verified strength. The stack is recorded in the report.\n\nPreset: identity_safe, catalog status 'candidate' (numerically equal to reference; mandatory character profile). Experimental: none switched on.\n\nScope: SFT only. Base: not verified in v1 (recognised by hash, no parity or gate run). Calibration stages B-D are not done. If a loader shows 'value not in list', the file is named or placed differently on your machine: open the combo and pick your file. A file in a subfolder of a models folder is listed with a backslash on Windows and a forward slash on Linux."
   ],
   "title": "MossPhoton multi_lora: versions, weights, status",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
